inals and Honors is worth 32 points, which is a good score. \n\nAnother consideration is the current game state. The next player has a Gang of T4, which might affect tile availability. But I'm not sure. \n\nIn conclusion, playing T7 seems to be the best move to aim for the All Terminals and Honors pattern.\n", "output": "Evaluation: Playing T7 removes the non-terminal tile, aligning the hand toward All Terminals and Honors (32 points) by retaining only W1, W9, T9, and F1. This maximizes potential for high-value patterns with available unshown tiles.\nReason: Discarding T7 simplifies the hand to terminals and honors (W1, W9, T9, F1), enabling pursuit of the 32-point All Terminals and Honors pattern. Unshown tiles (W1:3, W9:4, T9:4) provide ample opportunities to complete required pungs or pairs.\nAnswer: Play T7"}
